From c1c10155521f23b5bb7bab16799811c247407462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:37:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] feat(jvm): run a callback of the host in the exit hook

A server that ends through System.exit, as a server without the bridge
does on a signal, never returns from golem_jvm::run, so golem run has
no place to close what it opened, such as the store of the plugins,
whose last changes would then wait in the log of SQLite until the next
open.

HotSpot calls the exit hook after the shutdown hooks of Java, so the
server has stopped and saved by then, and a callback there is the last
code that runs before the process ends. golem_jvm::on_exit sets that
callback once, and the hook runs it after its line, behind a
catch_unwind that logs a panic, since the process ends either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016dYAZEa3eZnoeGd1c8FkBT
Signed-off-by: Florian Kleber <opensource@skytekx.com>
